>> title: Creamy Garlic Chicken
>> servings: 4
>> source: www.budgetbytes.com/creamy-garlic-chicken/

Using a #meat tenderizer or small saucepan{}, flatten @chicken breasts{2}(boneless, skinless).

Season each chicken breasts with @Italian seasoning{0.5%tsp}, @salt{0.5%tsp}, and @black pepper{0.5%tsp}. Then sprinkle @flour{0.25%cup} over both sides of the chicken breasts and rub it in until the chicken is evenly coated.

Heat a #skillet{} over medium heat and add @olive oil{2%Tbsp} and @butter{1%Tbsp}(divided). Once the skillet is hot, add the chicken and cook on each side until golden brown and cooked through (~{4%minutes} per side). Remove the cooked chicken to a clean plate and cover to keep warm.

While the chicken is cooking, peel @garlic{1}(whole bulb) and then carefully smash the cloves with the side of a #chef's knife{} by pressing down on the side of the knife with the heel of your hand.

Once the chicken is removed, to the same skillet add the remaining @butter{1%Tbsp}(divided), then add the smashed garlic cloves. Turn the heat down to medium-low and sauté the garlic for ~{3%minutes} or until lightly browned and fragrant. Make sure to stir the garlic frequently to prevent it from burning.

Next, pour in @chicken broth{1%cup} and @heavy cream{0.75%cup}, then add @garlic powder{0.5%tsp}. Stir and scrape up any brown bits from the bottom of the skillet. Allow the sauce to simmer in the skillet for ~{8-10%minutes}, or until it has reduced and thickened by about 50%. Taste the sauce at this point and add @salt{} and @ground black pepper{} if needed.

Finally, return the cooked chicken breasts to the skillet and spoon the creamy sauce over top. Allow the chicken to heat through. Serve with @parsley{}(chopped) if desired, and enjoy!